From 0638ba507c03be8cebbe383aa0d8475015f30875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:13:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(agents): two bug and two enhancement issues in
 flight at once

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 AGENTS.md | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 8ca3c8a8..4758277a 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -54,6 +54,18 @@ design context, never add work to them. Decisions still go to
   and take the highest priority first: `P0` (wrong output, gouge, crash,
   data loss) before `P1` (wrong behaviour a user hits) before `P2` (owed
   polish), then the oldest. User-reported bugs outrank owed work.
+- **Two lanes, two issues each** (user, 2026-11-07: "open up the issue
+  limit to 2 bugs 2 enhancements.. as we are now just working on the latest
+  issues and not the old ones"). At most four issues are worked at once: two
+  in the **bug lane** (label `bug`, or an unlabelled P0/P1 defect) and two in
+  the **enhancement lane** (label `enhancement`). An issue counts against its
+  lane from its claim until its PR merges, so one sitting `in-review` still
+  holds its slot. The bug lane picks by the order above. The enhancement lane
+  picks user-filed issues (no `source:agent`) first, then `P1` before `P2`,
+  then the oldest, so old owed work is not starved by fresh bugs. When a slot
+  frees, refill that lane at once. Each slot is its own worktree and branch
+  (check free disk first: each worktree's `target/` is 10-20 GB). An
+  enhancement PR is a `feat` and merges at the next minor cut.
 - **Start from the latest main, on a branch of its own** (user, 2026-11-07:
   "make sure we are on the latest main by pulling data from github then
   create a new branch to work off of"). Before the first edit:

